Qt 6
----
https://www.qt.io/
LGPLv3 (Qt Core, Qt Gui, Qt Network, Qt OpenGL, Qt Qml, Qt Quick; the QML
modules QtQuick.Controls and QtQuick.Layouts, loaded by the window at run time;
in the AppImage also what linuxdeploy-plugin-qt adds to those: Qt DBus, the xcb
and offscreen platform plugins, the platform theme and input context plugins).

Linked dynamically, as separate, replaceable libraries; Qt is not part of this
repository. `cmake --install` installs our own licence texts (these files,
LGPL-3.0.txt, GPL-3.0.txt) into Contents/Resources/licenses of roost.app or
share/licenses/roost; the .app and AppImage packages, which add Qt, carry them
the same way.
Qt sources: https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/ for the version named
in the release notes. No GPL-only Qt module is linked.


ICU
---
https://icu.unicode.org/
ICU licence (permissive, MIT-style; the Unicode data under the Unicode licence).
Version 73, as in the Qt the AppImage is built with.

AppImage only: libicuuc, libicui18n and libicudata, the libraries Qt Core of
the Qt build links; copied in with Qt, as separate libraries. The licence text
is usr/share/licenses/roost/ICU-LICENSE.txt of the AppImage (icu4c/LICENSE of
the release-73-2 tag, https://github.com/unicode-org/icu).

Libraries copied into the AppImage from the build machine (Ubuntu 24.04)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
linuxdeploy copies the libraries of the xcb platform plugin that a desktop may
lack, with the Debian copyright file of each package (the text of its licence)
into usr/share/doc/<package>/ of the AppImage. What every desktop has (GLib,
D-Bus, systemd, the compression, Kerberos, libpng and X11 libraries; the list
is packaging/linux/system-libraries.txt) is not carried: the AppImage uses the
ones of the machine it runs on. Not part of the macOS .app. Each is linked
dynamically and replaceable; the sources are those of the Ubuntu 24.04
packages.

